y the favorable side, both have 1500 contribution from the best outcome. But since B also has a large negative counterpart, and the reason says 'more favorable', it may still prefer A. So the reason could support A or be indifferent, depending on interpretation. But crucially, the information needed (maximum magnitude outcomes and their probabilities) is available.",
